+booking desk. Add boards or sails with `addEquipment({ id, kind, dailyPrice, hourlyPrice? })`, where
+`dailyPrice` is a non-negative integer number of euro cents per day and the optional `hourlyPrice` is
+a non-negative integer number of euro cents per hour. Rentals shorter than a day must start and end
+on whole UTC hours and require an hourly price; their price is the hourly price multiplied by the
+number of hours. Rentals lasting a day or longer use UTC midnight timestamps and daily pricing.
+Rentals lasting three days or longer receive a 10% discount from the full price; discounted totals
+are rounded to the nearest cent. `quote({ itemId, start, end })` calculates the price,
+`availability({ start, end, kind? })` returns the sorted IDs of equipment free for the whole period
+(optionally filtered to boards or sails), and `book(...)` reserves the item and returns its booking
+ID. The start is included and the end is exclusive, so a one-day rental ends at midnight on the
+following day. Equipment cannot have overlapping bookings. The service does not persist data after
+it is discarded. Cancellation is not implemented yet.
